            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "HomemakerSuzy"
            },
            "reviewBody": "So I looked at the ingredient list and then went to the kitchen...without writing down the measurements. What I made was this...just with altered proportions. I used ~3/4 C ice coffee (instant dissolved in a blend of milk / vanilla soy milk instead of water...this also accounts for the added milk), frozen banana (instead of banana + ice) and about 1/2 C of ice cream. Looks like I forgot the chocolate syrup. Oops. Well it tasted great! A nice way to have your morning cold coffee but get in some fruit as well!! It's easily justifiable as healthy b/c of the banana...just ignore the 1/2 C of ice cream! ;-)"
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
              "@type": "Rating",
              "ratingValue": "5"
            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "sweetdixie"
            },
            "reviewBody": "I personalized the recipe (seeing smoothies more as a protein shake opportunity). I used a frozen banana and omitted the ice. Half cup of unsweetened vanilla almond milk, half cup cold black coffee, 1 scoop vanilla Whey protein powder, 1 tsp. Cocoa powder, 2 packets Stevia (optional, tastes fine either way). Forget the ice cream and chocolate syrup. The frozen banana made it thick and creamy, and adds the perfect amount of sweetness! Seriously, a guilt-free \"milk shake\" that's GOOD for you. What could be better?!",
            "datePublished": "2016-05-23T14:39:06.843Z"
          },
          {
